Wed Oct 28 16:34:26 UTC 2026 - Ackerman-00 <noreply@example.com>

- Recommends: `vulkan-loader` is a Fedora package name and resolves to
  nothing on Tumbleweed (the SRPM is called vulkan-loader, the package
  is libvulkan1) - zypper silently dropped the weak dep. Use libvulkan1.
- The shipped binary talks to org.freedesktop.portal.* (file chooser,
  screen share) with no portal frontend declared; add weak Recommends on
  xdg-desktop-portal + xdg-desktop-portal-gtk.

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Wed Oct 28 16:25:00 UTC 2026 - Ackerman-00 <noreply@example.com>

- Stay on the stable channel: upstream publishes 0.20.2.1 with
  `prerelease: true` (2026-10-28T12:54Z), so the build shipped here for
  one cycle was a pre-release. Revert to the latest stable release
  0.20.1.1 (published 2026-10-21T14:34Z, `prerelease: false`).
- update.sh: derive the newest NON-prerelease GitHub release from the
  releases API (`prerelease == false and draft == false`, tag list as
  fallback) instead of sorting raw `git ls-remote` tags - a pre-release
  tag can no longer be promoted into the stable channel.

